{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When you beget children and children's children.</b> This section is joined to the matter of idolatry: that Israel is destined to serve idolatry in the land and to be exiled from it on account of this sin. Therefore it says כי תוליד and did not say אם תוליד, because it serves for the moment — that he reproves them now — and he prophesies concerning what will befall them in future generations." "<b>And you grow old in the land.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (darshu): this hints to them that they will be exiled at the end of 492 years, according to the numerical value of ונושנתם, for it is written (ibid. 6): ״ויהי בשמונים שנה וארבע מאות שנה לצאת בני ישראל מארץ מצרים ויבן הבית לה'״, and the Temple stood 410 years; take from them the 40 years in the wilderness, and 450 remain, and he advanced the exile by two years so that ״כי אבד תאבדון״ would not be fulfilled in them — and this is what is written (Daniel 9:14): ״וישקד ה׳ על הרעה ויביאה עלינו כי צדיק ה׳ אלהינו״ — He did righteousness for us by hastening the punishment to come two years before its time."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The word ונושתנם appears in the source as a transposed spelling of ונושנתם for the gematria calculation; rendered as written. The source citation '(שם ו)' refers to 1 Kings 6:1. The arithmetical chain (480 − 40 = 440; 440 − 410 + 2 = 492) is translated faithfully without correcting the working."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:25.750795720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}